⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Mildred Montag
node 451 · 451 · ⟦Mildred Montag:451:c765db⟧

WHO   — Mildred Montag — lost to the walls
WHAT  — The portrait of the drowned self: she calls the wall-characters ‘the family,’ cannot remember where she and Montag met, and turns him in.
WHERE — 451 · FAHRENHEIT 451  Framework inputs: Fahrenheit 451 (Ray Bradbury, 1953)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the warning's saddest face is the loved one already gone — anesthetised by screens, hollow and unreachable.
HOW   — By total immersion in interactive TV and earbud noise, soma-like pills, and a refusal to feel anything real.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I have a family in the walls and a sea in my ears — I can't remember where we met, and I can't sit in a quiet room, and I don't want to.

